1
00:02:18,530 --> 00:02:19,450
P'Hora.

2
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:24,520
What’s troubling you?

3
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:29,880
Last night, I had a dream about Sri.

4
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:39,170
Sri?

5
00:03:36,579 --> 00:03:37,940
What?

6
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:42,290
You dreamed that he returned the royal ring to you?

7
00:03:45,470 --> 00:03:46,420
Yes.

8
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:53,220
Is something going to happen to our son?

9
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:37,300
Do you know…

10
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:43,780
what hurts a person the most?

11
00:04:47,950 --> 00:04:49,000
You don’t want to answer?

12
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:52,460
Then let me tell you.

13
00:04:58,159 --> 00:05:02,660
It’s being betrayed by the one you love and trust.

14
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:07,270
The pain is unbearable.

15
00:05:09,610 --> 00:05:11,430
I loved and supported him.

16
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:17,460
I raised him with the same love and care as my own son.

17
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:22,780
I cherished him because he’s talented

18
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,290
and always humble.

19
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:29,770
He never put me in a difficult position.

20
00:05:31,610 --> 00:05:33,530
Someone like him is hard to find,

21
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:38,530
so I kept him close to me,

22
00:05:39,490 --> 00:05:43,310
but he became a thorn in my side

23
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:48,540
I have no other choice.

24
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:03,280
What are you waiting for?

25
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:06,530
Get out of my sight.

26
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:24,130
What do you want?

27
00:06:47,050 --> 00:06:48,210
P’Sri’s fate

28
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:50,880
is something that can’t be changed.

29
00:06:52,870 --> 00:06:54,250
But he’s remarkable.

30
00:06:55,630 --> 00:06:56,570
No matter where he goes,

31
00:06:57,610 --> 00:06:59,909
people will admire and love him.

32
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:06,430
Why does fate decide our destiny?

33
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:11,070
I didn’t believe it before.

34
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:14,170
I’m…

35
00:07:15,750 --> 00:07:17,190
afraid that one day,

36
00:07:20,050 --> 00:07:21,730
I won’t get to see you

37
00:07:23,070 --> 00:07:24,140
and P’Sri again.

38
00:08:29,310 --> 00:08:30,750
Sri, my son.

39
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:34,799
Why did it have to end like this?

40
00:08:40,570 --> 00:08:42,490
How much longer

41
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:46,400
until the King’s punishment is over?

42
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,850
Remember this.

43
00:09:02,070 --> 00:09:03,370
Be successful,

44
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:05,800
but don’t stand out.

45
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:08,850
It’ll only bring you trouble.

46
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:24,220
Don’t worry.

47
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,470
I’ll hurry back to take care of you

48
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:39,880
and repay His Majesty’s kindness.

49
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:47,750
Take care of yourselves, my boy.

50
00:09:49,450 --> 00:09:50,160
I will.

51
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,000
Dech.

52
00:10:00,990 --> 00:10:01,920
Gaew.

53
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:07,690
Escort P’Sri safely to Nakhon city.

54
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:09,830
Yes.

55
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,980
You committed a crime against the kingdom,

56
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:27,870
so you’ve been sent here.

57
00:11:28,710 --> 00:11:30,870
But your reputation

58
00:11:31,770 --> 00:11:32,550
as Sriprach,

59
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:35,040
the great poet,

60
00:11:35,770 --> 00:11:37,450
and your extraordinary talent,

61
00:11:38,910 --> 00:11:41,090
hasn’t disappeared because of your punishment.

62
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:43,590
So,

63
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:46,180
if you use your wisdom

64
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,850
and your gift with words

65
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:51,480
to do good for the people here,

66
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:53,460
that'd make me very happy.

67
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:02,320
Yes, my lord.

68
00:12:06,380 --> 00:12:07,430
From now on,

69
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,380
this place

70
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,630
will be your home.

71
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:28,370
Thank you,

72
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:29,810
Dech,

73
00:12:30,580 --> 00:12:31,290
Gaew,

74
00:12:32,850 --> 00:12:34,510
for escorting me all the way here.

75
00:12:38,430 --> 00:12:39,900
Will you be okay?

76
00:12:43,790 --> 00:12:45,740
Even if I’m not okay at first,

77
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:47,770
I’ll endure it.

78
00:12:49,670 --> 00:12:51,470
I don’t have any other choice.

79
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,200
Please take care of our parents for me.

80
00:13:07,490 --> 00:13:09,320
I wasn’t blessed enough

81
00:13:10,810 --> 00:13:12,690
to stay by their side until they grow old.

82
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:16,040
I’ll wait for the day you come home,

83
00:13:17,390 --> 00:13:19,580
then we’ll take care of them together.

84
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,500
P’Sri.

85
00:13:55,450 --> 00:13:57,780
Take good care of yourself.

86
00:13:59,370 --> 00:14:00,630
Don’t trust anyone.

87
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:04,100
Don’t make any mistakes.

88
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,550
Be careful.

89
00:14:08,630 --> 00:14:09,570
I’m worried about you.

90
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,920
Thank you for your concern.

91
00:14:29,510 --> 00:14:30,920
You too.

92
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:35,340
Even though you know so much,

93
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:39,760
we can’t change fate however we want.

94
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,610
I hope

95
00:14:46,370 --> 00:14:47,240
you and Dech

96
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:50,840
live happy lives.

97
00:14:52,530 --> 00:14:54,660
Don’t end up being separated like me.

98
00:15:00,610 --> 00:15:01,860
I should get going now, P’Sri.

99
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:07,810
I know the pain and worry won’t disappear overnight,

100
00:16:10,170 --> 00:16:12,080
but you have to stay strong for P’Sri.

101
00:16:12,990 --> 00:16:14,360
So he won’t have to worry about you.

102
00:16:16,530 --> 00:16:17,870
Now that we’re parting,

103
00:16:19,130 --> 00:16:20,640
I don’t know if we’ll ever meet again.

104
00:16:22,410 --> 00:16:23,620
Of course we will.

105
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:26,450
P’Sri can’t come see us,

106
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:29,040
but we can always go see him.

107
00:16:35,670 --> 00:16:36,920
I’m so lucky

108
00:16:37,930 --> 00:16:39,660
to have you by my side.

109
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:43,540
I promise

110
00:16:44,370 --> 00:16:45,780
I’ll be strong again soon.

111
00:16:47,870 --> 00:16:48,950
I need just one thing.

112
00:16:50,580 --> 00:16:52,420
Please don’t ever leave me.

113
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,530
Stay by my side.

114
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,110
Can you promise me?

115
00:17:33,410 --> 00:17:34,440
I promise.

116
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:47,320
I love you.

117
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:50,410
Same here.

118
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,780
I love you too, Muen Muen.

119
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:57,770
You’re talking funny again.

120
00:18:15,890 --> 00:18:17,250
Now that we’re by the sea,

121
00:18:18,430 --> 00:18:21,900
do you know how to ride the waves?

122
00:18:23,790 --> 00:18:25,120
Ride the waves?

123
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,160
What does that mean, P’Muen?

124
00:21:27,670 --> 00:21:29,730
So this is riding the waves.

125
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,370
The Lovers.

126
00:22:00,470 --> 00:22:02,630
It means you and this person

127
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,600
choose each other.

128
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:07,900
Not just with your hearts,

129
00:22:08,770 --> 00:22:11,400
but with your bodies and fate as well.

130
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:16,130
From now on, your love will no longer be a secret.

131
00:22:17,530 --> 00:22:19,030
And every choice you make

132
00:22:20,100 --> 00:22:21,800
comes with a price.

133
00:22:39,100 --> 00:22:41,630
The agarwood still hasn’t arrived. It’s rare these days.

134
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:43,600
Let me know

135
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:44,600
as soon as it comes in,

136
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:45,830
Yes, my lord.

137
00:22:56,930 --> 00:22:57,970
Reung!

138
00:23:00,030 --> 00:23:02,730
Aren’t you tired of following me all day?

139
00:23:03,570 --> 00:23:05,830
I need time to choose the medicine.

140
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:09,800
Well,

141
00:23:10,570 --> 00:23:12,130
if I get to spend time with you,

142
00:23:12,830 --> 00:23:14,470
I don’t mind.

143
00:23:14,470 --> 00:23:15,970
I’m not tired at all.

144
00:23:31,630 --> 00:23:32,670
Wait.

145
00:23:32,670 --> 00:23:33,770
What’s that smell?

146
00:23:34,970 --> 00:23:36,470
Is it the herbs,

147
00:23:37,700 --> 00:23:39,370
or your scent?

148
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:42,230
Reung!

149
00:23:43,770 --> 00:23:44,900
Be careful.

150
00:24:00,970 --> 00:24:02,530
If anyone gets suspicious,

151
00:24:02,930 --> 00:24:04,470
we’ll be in trouble.

152
00:24:06,630 --> 00:24:08,100
No one is watching,

153
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:09,170
Wad.

154
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:13,230
No one, indeed.

155
00:24:26,970 --> 00:24:28,000
Hm.

156
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:30,270
Moo Sarong is really delicious.

157
00:24:30,270 --> 00:24:31,430
Just as good as they say.

158
00:24:38,570 --> 00:24:40,030
Jumpa.

159
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:41,730
Have you heard?

160
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:46,130
King Narai has issued a royal decree

161
00:24:46,130 --> 00:24:47,930
appointing Okya-Kosa Thibodi

162
00:24:47,930 --> 00:24:51,000
as Chaopraya-Kosathibodi,

163
00:24:51,230 --> 00:24:54,570
ruling over both the inner and outer courts

164
00:24:54,900 --> 00:24:58,270
in matters of foreign trade.

165
00:24:58,830 --> 00:25:02,130
That's wonderful news, P’Hora.

166
00:25:02,870 --> 00:25:05,030
I’m happy for you.

167
00:25:07,100 --> 00:25:07,930
Also,

168
00:25:07,930 --> 00:25:11,530
His Majesty has appointed our Dech

169
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:16,070
as Okkhun-Sriwisanwaja.

170
00:25:16,070 --> 00:25:18,130
Is this true?

171
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:22,130
We have so much good news today.

172
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:26,400
No words can describe how excited I am.

173
00:25:28,170 --> 00:25:28,970
Prik.

174
00:25:28,970 --> 00:25:29,500
Yes.

175
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:31,630
I’m the mother of an Okkhun now.

176
00:25:32,070 --> 00:25:33,800
Congratulations, my lady.

177
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:36,330
That’s not all.

178
00:25:36,730 --> 00:25:38,970
His Majesty has also ordered Dech and me

179
00:25:39,430 --> 00:25:41,470
to join the Siamese embassy

180
00:25:41,630 --> 00:25:43,800
to establish friendly ties

181
00:25:43,800 --> 00:25:46,900
with King Louis XIV in France

182
00:25:46,900 --> 00:25:48,600
in three months.

183
00:25:54,070 --> 00:25:55,600
So the time has finally come.

184
00:26:04,530 --> 00:26:05,530
P’Muen!

185
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:10,070
I want to congratulate you

186
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:12,200
on going to France.

187
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,170
Hold on.

188
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:17,170
I’ve been promoted to Khun now.

189
00:26:17,570 --> 00:26:18,570
That’s right.

190
00:26:19,300 --> 00:26:20,300
P’Khun.

191
00:26:20,930 --> 00:26:23,000
Okkhun-Sriwisanwaja.

192
00:26:27,270 --> 00:26:29,800
It's a nice season to go to France.

193
00:26:30,670 --> 00:26:32,100
It won’t be too cold,

194
00:26:32,100 --> 00:26:33,570
and there’s no snow.

195
00:26:35,100 --> 00:26:36,430
How do you know?

196
00:26:36,870 --> 00:26:38,000
Have you been there?

197
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:40,270
Uh…

198
00:26:42,230 --> 00:26:43,200
No.

199
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:44,930
Just a guess.

200
00:26:48,270 --> 00:26:50,130
When you return from France,

201
00:26:50,730 --> 00:26:52,730
I might not be here anymore.

202
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,270
What do you mean?

203
00:26:55,970 --> 00:26:57,000
Nothing.

204
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,270
I was just saying.

205
00:27:27,430 --> 00:27:29,200
You’re going to sleep with me?

206
00:27:29,870 --> 00:27:31,130
Aren’t you afraid?

207
00:27:32,230 --> 00:27:33,570
Afraid of what?

208
00:27:34,730 --> 00:27:36,130
If I were afraid of anything,

209
00:27:36,570 --> 00:27:38,100
I’d be more afraid

210
00:27:38,470 --> 00:27:41,670
of not having you by my side.

211
00:27:56,670 --> 00:27:57,700
Come here,

212
00:27:57,700 --> 00:27:58,830
Gaew.

213
00:28:30,570 --> 00:28:32,200
P’Khun,

214
00:28:32,530 --> 00:28:34,200
do you want to know about

215
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:35,470
the place I came from?

216
00:28:36,530 --> 00:28:39,270
I want to know everything about you.

217
00:28:41,670 --> 00:28:43,530
The place I came from

218
00:28:45,130 --> 00:28:46,670
is filled with lights.

219
00:28:48,570 --> 00:28:50,630
Buildings reaching the sky.

220
00:28:52,270 --> 00:28:55,500
Trains above the streets.

221
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:59,130
Subways underground.

222
00:29:00,930 --> 00:29:02,800
People rushing everywhere.

223
00:29:05,070 --> 00:29:06,930
It’s completely different from here.

224
00:29:08,930 --> 00:29:10,500
The place you came from

225
00:29:11,100 --> 00:29:12,670
sounds very strange.

226
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:16,800
Come to think of it,

227
00:29:16,800 --> 00:29:18,200
it’s really strange, P’Khun.

228
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:21,800
I appeared here

229
00:29:22,170 --> 00:29:23,900
all of a sudden.

230
00:29:25,930 --> 00:29:28,500
No matter how much I think about it,

231
00:29:29,270 --> 00:29:30,600
I can’t figure out

232
00:29:31,470 --> 00:29:34,270
why I ended up here with you.

233
00:29:37,930 --> 00:29:39,130
Perhaps

234
00:29:40,230 --> 00:29:42,070
it’s because of destiny.

235
00:29:55,900 --> 00:29:58,200
Destiny?

236
00:29:58,200 --> 00:29:59,730
It could be.

237
00:30:01,330 --> 00:30:03,200
But...

238
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:04,830
you said that

239
00:30:06,100 --> 00:30:08,330
I appeared here

240
00:30:08,330 --> 00:30:11,070
after you performed the Krishna Kali spell.

241
00:30:13,370 --> 00:30:14,900
I think

242
00:30:16,270 --> 00:30:18,870
that spell somehow brought me here.

243
00:30:28,770 --> 00:30:30,300
Then,

244
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:33,830
if you perform it again,

245
00:30:36,130 --> 00:30:38,530
I might be able to return home, right?

246
00:30:42,970 --> 00:30:43,970
P’Khun?

247
00:30:45,430 --> 00:30:46,700
P’Khun?

248
00:30:46,700 --> 00:30:48,700
Go to sleep, Gaew.

249
00:31:40,170 --> 00:31:42,470
Okya-Wichayen has grown far too powerful

250
00:31:42,470 --> 00:31:44,400
and is acting beyond his authority.

251
00:31:44,630 --> 00:31:47,500
He’s established a foreign volunteer army in Bangkok,

252
00:31:47,970 --> 00:31:50,400
stockpiled weapons and artillery,

253
00:31:51,230 --> 00:31:53,390
and let foreigners guard the fortresses

254
00:31:53,390 --> 00:31:54,740
instead of Ayutthaya’s men.

255
00:31:55,300 --> 00:31:57,100
He’s gone too far.

256
00:31:57,900 --> 00:31:59,670
He’s doing this to protect his power,

257
00:32:00,270 --> 00:32:02,430
not the peace of the kingdom.

258
00:32:03,170 --> 00:32:04,270
Isn’t that right?

259
00:32:04,970 --> 00:32:07,170
If we let him continue,

260
00:32:07,170 --> 00:32:08,300
it will end badly.

261
00:32:08,570 --> 00:32:09,630
Right now,

262
00:32:10,070 --> 00:32:11,270
he holds enormous power

263
00:32:11,900 --> 00:32:13,280
and has weapons at his disposal.

264
00:32:13,530 --> 00:32:15,630
We must tread carefully.

265
00:32:16,970 --> 00:32:18,230
I agree.

266
00:32:19,530 --> 00:32:21,670
That’s why we need clear evidence

267
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:24,030
to bring him to justice.

268
00:32:24,630 --> 00:32:27,300
I won’t let anything happen

269
00:32:27,770 --> 00:32:29,470
to this kingdom.

270
00:32:32,700 --> 00:32:34,100
We must act quickly, Reung.

271
00:32:34,830 --> 00:32:36,770
I’ll help you.

272
00:33:15,130 --> 00:33:16,300
Search everywhere.

273
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:40,130
Reung.

274
00:33:40,130 --> 00:33:41,230
I found it.

275
00:33:57,970 --> 00:34:00,500
The English weapons trade records.

276
00:34:02,070 --> 00:34:04,130
Those English men betrayed me.

277
00:34:06,670 --> 00:34:07,670
I may have

278
00:34:08,030 --> 00:34:10,230
take an advantage of my position,

279
00:34:11,100 --> 00:34:13,370
but I never plundered like they did.

280
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,199
Never.

281
00:34:16,170 --> 00:34:20,030
I will not be take an advantage of anymore!

282
00:34:23,030 --> 00:34:25,969
They believe they have proof to bring me down.

283
00:34:27,429 --> 00:34:29,929
We must eliminate the evidence

284
00:34:29,929 --> 00:34:31,429
before they act!

285
00:34:32,100 --> 00:34:33,100
Yes, sir.

286
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:41,030
Then let’s submit a petition

287
00:34:41,030 --> 00:34:43,070
against this kingdom's traitor.

288
00:34:48,630 --> 00:34:49,400
Someone’s coming.

289
00:34:50,570 --> 00:34:51,500
Hurry.

290
00:34:51,500 --> 00:34:52,770
Who are you guys?

291
00:34:52,770 --> 00:34:53,870
Move!

292
00:34:56,929 --> 00:34:58,000
Stop!

293
00:35:07,930 --> 00:35:09,200
Sir!

294
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:16,270
Our English weapons trade records

295
00:35:16,270 --> 00:35:18,170
are missing.

296
00:35:19,830 --> 00:35:21,270
Bring them to me.

297
00:35:36,700 --> 00:35:37,770
Gaew.

298
00:35:38,530 --> 00:35:39,870
Lord Khun.

299
00:35:40,900 --> 00:35:41,830
Muen Reung.

300
00:35:41,830 --> 00:35:43,170
What happened to P’Khun?

301
00:35:43,900 --> 00:35:44,830
Dech was shot

302
00:35:44,830 --> 00:35:47,200
while searching for evidence against Okya-Wichayen.

303
00:35:47,470 --> 00:35:48,570
He was shot?

304
00:35:49,730 --> 00:35:51,270
Let's take him to his room.

305
00:35:51,600 --> 00:35:52,600
Follow me.

306
00:35:56,400 --> 00:35:57,130
Be careful, Dech.

307
00:35:57,130 --> 00:35:58,400
Watch out, Reung.

308
00:36:01,830 --> 00:36:02,830
Pin, support him.

309
00:36:02,830 --> 00:36:03,870
Yes, sir.

310
00:36:13,630 --> 00:36:14,630
The bullet is inside.

311
00:36:14,630 --> 00:36:15,970
We need to operate now.

312
00:36:16,670 --> 00:36:17,700
Pin, Yam.

313
00:36:17,700 --> 00:36:19,400
Go get Wad to help Dech.

314
00:36:19,770 --> 00:36:20,730
Yes, sir.

315
00:36:20,730 --> 00:36:21,870
No!

316
00:36:21,870 --> 00:36:23,730
There’s no time. I’ll do it.

317
00:36:23,730 --> 00:36:24,830
But the wound is severe.

318
00:36:24,830 --> 00:36:26,370
Let Wad handle it.

319
00:36:26,830 --> 00:36:27,530
Go quickly!

320
00:36:27,530 --> 00:36:28,830
Trust Gaew.

321
00:36:30,130 --> 00:36:31,400
Pin, Yam.

322
00:36:31,400 --> 00:36:32,670
Prepare the instruments.

323
00:36:32,670 --> 00:36:33,870
Yes, sir.

324
00:37:29,500 --> 00:37:30,730
P’Khun.

325
00:37:30,730 --> 00:37:32,130
Please hold on.

326
00:38:21,070 --> 00:38:23,100
You’re safe now, P’Khun.

327
00:38:34,170 --> 00:38:35,300
Reung.

328
00:38:35,300 --> 00:38:36,730
I’m safe.

329
00:38:37,730 --> 00:38:39,330
Thank you, Gaew.

330
00:38:39,700 --> 00:38:40,800
No problem.

331
00:38:41,970 --> 00:38:43,500
What a relief.

332
00:38:48,770 --> 00:38:51,070
What about the records?

333
00:38:51,530 --> 00:38:52,530
What’s next?

334
00:38:52,530 --> 00:38:53,670
Tomorrow,

335
00:38:53,670 --> 00:38:55,670
I’ll report this to Father

336
00:38:56,630 --> 00:38:58,470
before presenting these records

337
00:38:58,470 --> 00:39:00,630
to King Narai.

338
00:39:03,370 --> 00:39:04,900
Very well, Dech.

339
00:39:06,500 --> 00:39:07,570
My lord,

340
00:39:07,970 --> 00:39:09,800
you should change first.

341
00:39:10,330 --> 00:39:12,030
I’ll take care of him.

342
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:13,900
Tonight,

343
00:39:13,900 --> 00:39:16,300
I’ll stay by his side and look after him.

344
00:39:16,800 --> 00:39:18,030
Yes, sir.

345
00:40:17,470 --> 00:40:18,630
Gaew.

346
00:40:48,800 --> 00:40:49,900
Pin, Yam!

347
00:40:51,030 --> 00:40:52,230
Yes?

348
00:40:54,970 --> 00:40:56,370
What happened?

349
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:59,070
Uh…

350
00:40:59,070 --> 00:41:02,230
Answer me now!

351
00:41:02,500 --> 00:41:04,030
Uh…

352
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:06,570
Lord Khun was shot.

353
00:41:07,100 --> 00:41:08,130
Good heavens!

354
00:41:10,630 --> 00:41:11,330
Ah.

355
00:41:11,330 --> 00:41:12,430
My lady!

356
00:41:12,430 --> 00:41:13,830
Jumpa!

357
00:41:13,830 --> 00:41:15,950
My lady!

358
00:41:24,270 --> 00:41:25,570
P’Khun?

359
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:28,600
Are you tired?

360
00:41:29,830 --> 00:41:31,530
You dressed my wound

361
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:34,770
and watched over me all night.

362
00:41:37,170 --> 00:41:38,470
I’m not tired.

363
00:41:39,370 --> 00:41:40,400
And you?

364
00:41:40,800 --> 00:41:42,000
How are you feeling?

365
00:41:43,400 --> 00:41:44,530
I…

366
00:41:45,070 --> 00:41:46,070
I’m fine.

367
00:41:50,270 --> 00:41:51,500
My lord!

368
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:57,970
Please come to the main hall immediately.

369
00:41:58,400 --> 00:41:59,670
What happened?

370
00:42:00,030 --> 00:42:01,900
Lady Jumpa fainted

371
00:42:02,700 --> 00:42:05,800
after hearing you were shot.

372
00:42:14,430 --> 00:42:15,470
Dech.

373
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:17,130
Uh…

374
00:42:17,130 --> 00:42:18,430
I’m all right now

375
00:42:18,970 --> 00:42:20,500
thanks to Gaew.

376
00:42:26,470 --> 00:42:28,530
Thank you so much, Gaew,

377
00:42:28,530 --> 00:42:30,900
for saving my son.

378
00:42:31,530 --> 00:42:33,170
Without you,

379
00:42:33,170 --> 00:42:35,100
Dech wouldn’t have survived.

380
00:42:35,870 --> 00:42:37,700
I’m so grateful.

381
00:42:38,130 --> 00:42:40,600
I owe you a debt, Gaew.

382
00:42:41,030 --> 00:42:42,730
What debt are you talking about?

383
00:42:43,530 --> 00:42:45,330
I helped P’Khun because I wanted to.

384
00:42:50,270 --> 00:42:52,700
I can’t lose him either.

385
00:42:55,570 --> 00:42:57,130
Dech.

386
00:42:57,470 --> 00:43:00,000
Why did you keep it from me?

387
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:02,000
We already lost Sri.

388
00:43:02,370 --> 00:43:05,000
I don’t want to lose you too.

389
00:43:06,100 --> 00:43:07,500
I’m sorry, Father,

390
00:43:07,830 --> 00:43:09,130
Mother,

391
00:43:09,700 --> 00:43:11,770
for acting without thinking.

392
00:43:12,070 --> 00:43:13,330
Reung and I

393
00:43:13,330 --> 00:43:14,670
saw an opportunity,

394
00:43:15,870 --> 00:43:17,430
so we acted quickly.

395
00:43:18,670 --> 00:43:21,530
Make sure everyone who knows about this

396
00:43:21,530 --> 00:43:23,700
keeps completely silent.

397
00:43:24,630 --> 00:43:25,700
Yes.

398
00:43:28,030 --> 00:43:28,970
Father.

399
00:43:28,970 --> 00:43:29,970
Hm?

400
00:43:29,970 --> 00:43:30,970
Today,

401
00:43:31,800 --> 00:43:33,770
I’ll request an audience with King Narai.

402
00:43:34,370 --> 00:43:36,130
I'll present the evidence

403
00:43:36,130 --> 00:43:37,800
and petition His Majesty

404
00:43:38,070 --> 00:43:40,100
against Okya-Wichayen.

405
00:43:40,600 --> 00:43:42,730
We cannot allow him

406
00:43:43,170 --> 00:43:45,330
to wield power over His Majesty.

407
00:43:47,370 --> 00:43:48,370
Good.

408
00:43:49,970 --> 00:43:51,830
Does Luang Sorasak know about this?

409
00:43:52,670 --> 00:43:54,030
No.

410
00:43:54,030 --> 00:43:55,400
Only Reung and I know.

411
00:43:57,030 --> 00:43:59,870
Whatever happens, don’t let him find out.

412
00:44:01,370 --> 00:44:02,600
Yes, Father.

413
00:44:10,100 --> 00:44:12,300
Chaopraya-Kosathibodi has arrived.

414
00:44:18,300 --> 00:44:19,570
I bring news

415
00:44:20,130 --> 00:44:21,530
about Lord Phra Sriprach.

416
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:35,430
Phraya Nakhon has ordered

417
00:44:40,470 --> 00:44:41,870
his execution.

418
00:44:43,530 --> 00:44:45,630
Phra Sriprach…

419
00:44:50,170 --> 00:44:51,800
is dead

420
00:44:54,900 --> 00:44:58,530
in Nakhon Si Thammarat.

421
00:45:03,430 --> 00:45:04,800
Lord…

422
00:45:06,200 --> 00:45:09,270
Phra Sriprach…

423
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:15,170
Your Highness.

424
00:45:17,830 --> 00:45:19,030
Your Highness.

425
00:45:22,900 --> 00:45:23,970
Why?

426
00:45:24,770 --> 00:45:27,500
Phraya Nakhon was enraged.

427
00:45:28,570 --> 00:45:30,470
He believed that Lord Phra Sriprach

428
00:45:31,630 --> 00:45:34,430
had an affair with his consort,

429
00:45:35,530 --> 00:45:38,300
so he ordered his execution.

430
00:45:43,370 --> 00:45:45,470
My Sri.

431
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:49,630
My son.

432
00:46:38,570 --> 00:46:40,070
Do you know

433
00:46:40,070 --> 00:46:42,130
what you’ve done?

434
00:46:42,770 --> 00:46:44,900
You disobeyed me.

435
00:46:44,900 --> 00:46:46,900
You killed my man.

436
00:46:47,370 --> 00:46:49,430
If Sri was to die,

437
00:46:49,830 --> 00:46:51,600
it should have been by my order,

438
00:46:52,170 --> 00:46:53,800
not by someone like you!

439
00:46:54,700 --> 00:46:56,800
I never ordered his death!

440
00:46:57,370 --> 00:47:00,070
Why did you let your anger get the better of you?

441
00:47:05,070 --> 00:47:08,400
I have no excuses, Your Majesty.

442
00:47:10,300 --> 00:47:12,470
It was not out of arrogance,

443
00:47:14,470 --> 00:47:16,970
but I humbly accept responsibility

444
00:47:18,270 --> 00:47:21,570
for this unforgivable act.

445
00:47:31,870 --> 00:47:33,400
At least you know what you’ve done.

446
00:47:34,030 --> 00:47:36,500
But there will be no forgiveness.

447
00:47:37,070 --> 00:47:39,230
Since you ordered Sri’s death,

448
00:47:39,870 --> 00:47:41,070
then

449
00:47:41,070 --> 00:47:44,170
I shall order your execution!

450
00:47:47,630 --> 00:47:49,770
I humbly accept your verdict,

451
00:47:50,330 --> 00:47:51,500
Your Majesty.

452
00:48:08,530 --> 00:48:11,670
If one day you learns that I’m innocent,

453
00:48:16,130 --> 00:48:18,100
you will reap what you have sown.

454
00:48:45,070 --> 00:48:46,930
Love the right person,

455
00:48:47,400 --> 00:48:48,570
Reung.

456
00:48:50,030 --> 00:48:53,130
Can you teach me the Krishna Kali spell?

457
00:48:54,470 --> 00:48:56,130
Having you right here

458
00:48:56,130 --> 00:48:57,800
but being unable to get close

459
00:48:57,800 --> 00:48:59,430
is even more painful.

460
00:49:03,170 --> 00:49:04,200
Hey!

461
00:49:05,800 --> 00:49:07,100
P’Khun!

462
00:49:14,600 --> 00:49:16,230
I appeared here

463
00:49:16,770 --> 00:49:19,500
after you performed the Krishna Kali spell.

464
00:49:21,170 --> 00:49:23,400
if you perform it again,

465
00:49:23,800 --> 00:49:26,130
I might be able to return home, right?

466
00:49:26,800 --> 00:49:28,700
Go to sleep, Gaew.
